<p>This policy explains how we handle the personal data you send us through this website, in line with the Law on Personal Data Protection (2020).</p>

<h2>Who is responsible</h2>
<p>The controller is {{ site.operator.en }}, Tošo Arsov 32, 2000 Štip, North Macedonia, which runs Hotel Oaza at the same address. You can reach us at <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a> or on <a href="{% telHref %}">{{ site.phone.display }}</a>.</p>

<h2>What we collect and why</h2>
<p>When you send an enquiry, the form collects your name and email address and, if you give them, your phone number, company and message, together with the choices you make in the form: the type of stay or event, the dates, the number of guests, the room type and whether you need an overnight stay. It also records which page you sent it from, the page language and, if you arrived from an advertisement, the campaign details in the link (its source, medium and campaign name). We use this only to answer your enquiry and to prepare an offer. We process it because you asked us for an offer: it is needed to take the steps you request before a booking.</p>

<h2>Who receives it</h2>
<p>Your enquiry is sent by email to the hotel's reception. We do not sell it or pass it to anyone else. The website itself does not store enquiries. To limit how many enquiries can come from one connection, the server keeps a scrambled (hashed) form of your IP address with the times of your enquiries for one hour; older entries are deleted the next time the counter is updated. Like any web host, our hosting provider's servers also keep technical access logs, including IP addresses, to run the site and keep it secure.</p>

<h2>How long we keep it</h2>
<p>We keep enquiry emails for 12 months after the last message in the conversation, and then delete them. If the enquiry leads to a booking, invoices and payment records are kept for as long as accounting and tax law requires.</p>

<h2>Card payments</h2>
<p>Cards are charged on the pages of cPay (CaSys), not on this website: the card number never reaches us and we do not store it. For each charge the server keeps a record with the reservation number, the amount, the time, the result and cPay's reference. We keep these records for 18 months, and the technical notices cPay sends about each payment for 90 days; then they are deleted. They are kept on the hotel's hosting account and are not publicly accessible. To limit how many requests can come from one connection to the addresses that receive cPay's notices, the server keeps a hashed form of the IP address there too, for one hour.</p>

<h2>Other services</h2>
<p>Every page loads its typefaces from Google Fonts, so your browser connects to Google's servers, which see your IP address. Maps on this website load from Google Maps only when you choose to show them; Google then also receives your IP address and may set its own cookies. Google may process this data outside North Macedonia, including in the United States. The Viber and WhatsApp links open those apps, and their own privacy policies apply to the messages you send there.</p>

<h2>Your rights</h2>
<p>You can ask to see the personal data we hold about you, to correct or delete it, to receive it in a portable form, and to restrict or object to its use. Write to <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>.</p>

<h2>Complaints</h2>
<p>If you think we have handled your data unlawfully, you can complain to the Personal Data Protection Agency (АЗЛП): <a href="https://azlp.mk/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">azlp.mk<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>.</p>
